  <reporting-org ref="GB-CHC-202918" type="21">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Oxfam GB</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency Flood Response in Sindh &amp; Baluchistan_2022</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The primary objective of the project is to provide rapid lifesaving assistance to flood -affected communities, primarily focused on vulnerable women and children in districts Naseerabad, and Jafferabad of Balochistan province. Based upon the Rapid Need Assessment (RNA) report of Provincial Disaster Management Authority (PDMA) 78% population is of dire need of food assistance. In this regard Tameer e Khalq Foundation (TKF) with the financial support of OXFAM will be responding to the most immediate needs through integrated food security, Water Sanitation and Hygiene (WASH) and protection services alongside cash assistance to flood -affected communities of the targeted districts. These will be supported by protection activities, including the establishment of women and girls safe spaces to ensure primary hygiene and psychosocial needs.</narrative>
  </description>
